module stage0_boundary_add_probe

// THE COMMITTED SPECIMEN FOR THE STORAGE-READ SEAM, AND ONLY THAT SEAM.
//
// What this file is read by is v2.test.self_host.stage0_production_target's read claim: the path
// reaches source_ref_for_observed_storage_path, source_root_ingest_from_source_refs verifies the
// bytes against the ref's content hash, and the claim asserts that the source the ingest carries
// contains this declaration. Its discriminating sibling reads a path no file occupies and requires
// a refusal rather than an answer, which is why this file's own content is not that claim's
// subject and editing the prose around this declaration cannot break it. The door's own
// specimen carries its module source inline (direct_rust_door_fixture
// direct_rust_door_dag_module_source), so nothing else in the corpus exercises that route over a
// file actually on disk.
//
// IT IS NOT INGESTED, ASSEMBLED, INFERRED OR EMITTED BY ANY CLAIM, and this sentence is here
// because an earlier revision of it said otherwise. That revision was true when written -- the
// three emission claims did run the full disk-to-emit walk over this file -- and stopped being
// true when those claims moved onto the door's warm-shared resolved specimen to fit the floor's
// per-claim ceiling. An annotation describing a route no claim executes is the
// specification-without-execution DESIGN section 5 names, so the two facts are now separate on
// purpose: the READ is claimed here over a real file, and the two stage0 target-profile
// SELECTIONS are claimed over the shared specimen. Neither claim covers the other, and the file
// carries the fact it is actually the subject of.
//
// The declaration is deliberately the shape the production composition admits (one arrow), so
// that if a future change wants the composed route back it can take this file whole. What this
// specimen is NOT is the acceptance subject for the production flip: that is the real corpus
// module gunbc.rust_decl_type_overlay, and it does not emit yet.

fn probe_add(x: Int, y: Int) -> Int { x + y }
